&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Robotics &amp;amp; Mechatronics Teams at Agile Robots&lt;/strong&gt; are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;(Senior) Electronics Engineer (m/f/d)&lt;/strong&gt; who will help develop PCB-level electronics for our robot arms, from safety-circuit design through to production-ready schematics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PCB Design:&lt;/strong&gt; Create and review schematics, PCB layouts, and wiring diagrams for production, from initial concept through manufacturing-ready output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Safety Circuits:&lt;/strong&gt; Design and implement safety circuits and fail-safe mechanisms for the robot&#39;s electronics, working within established safety requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Component Selection:&lt;/strong&gt; Select and integrate electronic components (motors, drivers, sensors, power systems) that meet the robot&#39;s performance and reliability requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Test Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Design in-house test devices and write test cases for the electronics subsystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hardware Debugging:&lt;/strong&gt; Troubleshoot and resolve electrical and electronics issues on the physical robot, working directly with firmware, software, and mechanics engineers when a fault crosses disciplines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documentation:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and maintain electrical documentation, including BOMs, test procedures, and compliance reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering Background:&lt;/strong&gt; Degree in Electrical Engineering, Electronics, or a related field, or an equivalent combination of training and hands-on experience designing electronics for robotic or industrial systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-On Build:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience building and debugging electronics, including schematic capture and PCB layout in Altium Designer, microcontroller programming, and signal debugging using oscilloscopes and logic analyzers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Safety Standards:&lt;/strong&gt; Working knowledge of safety standards for high-voltage and high-current electronics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Power Electronics:&lt;/strong&gt; Working knowledge of power electronics for robotic systems, including PMSM motor control, DC/DC converters, battery management, and thermal design for power components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication Protocols:&lt;/strong&gt; Working understanding of communication protocols used in robotic and embedded systems, including CAN, SPI, I2C, and Ethernet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Beneficial Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Harness Design:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience with harness design and cable management for moving systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SolidWorks Electrical:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience with SolidWorks Electrical for wiring and harness documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Functional Safety:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience working on functional safety projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Test Specifications:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience writing requirements and test case specifications, and implementing the resulting tests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Software Tools:&lt;/strong&gt; Familiarity with common software engineering tools such as git.&lt;/li&gt;
